---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 1,
        "name": "Home",
        "item": "https://www.alluviumbi.com/"
      },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 2,
        "name": "Services",
        "item": "https://www.alluviumbi.com/services"
      },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 3,
        "name": "Managed Advisory Retainer",
        "item": "https://www.alluviumbi.com/managed-advisory-retainer"
      }
    ]
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Keep one version of the report current | Alluvium"
  description="After go-live the Power BI report goes stale or splits into copies. A retainer keeps one version current without a large team on staff."
  canonicalPath="/managed-advisory-retainer"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="service-fold">
<article>
<header class="hero"><div class="wrap">
<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><a href="/services">Services</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><span>Managed Advisory Retainer</span></nav>
<p class="kicker">Managed Advisory Retainer</p>
<h1>Keep one version of the report current</h1>
<p class="lede">After go-live the report goes stale, or it splits into copies. We keep one version current, without a large team on staff to watch it.</p>
<p class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a Session</a></p>
</div></header>
<section class="band"><div class="wrap">
<h2>The project ends, and the report keeps changing</h2>
<p>Someone changes a definition. Who can see which rows still matches last year. The refresh finishes when it finishes, and the meeting has already started.</p>
<p>Then two people answer the same question from two copies. Steady attention on one version stops that. You can keep the report honest without hiring a bench of specialists.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="band band-alt"><div class="wrap">
<h2>The same report, month after month</h2>
<p>Copies sit off to the side. The report on the line is the one people still open.</p>
<figure class="diagram"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 640 240" role="img" aria-label="One report stays on a line. Two copies sit off to the side.">
<line x1="40" y1="120" x2="600" y2="120" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
<rect x="250" y="36" width="140" height="168" rx="4" fill="#e7f1f8" stroke="#1c1c1c" stroke-width="2.5"/>
<rect x="270" y="58" width="100" height="16" fill="#397fb0"/>
<rect x="270" y="88" width="22" height="70" fill="#1c1c1c"/>
<rect x="302" y="110" width="22" height="48" fill="#397fb0"/>
<rect x="334" y="98" width="22" height="60" fill="#397fb0" opacity="0.75"/>
<circle cx="320" cy="120" r="8" fill="#1c1c1c"/>
<rect x="36" y="150" width="110" height="70" rx="3" fill="#f4f7fa" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="2"/>
<line x1="50" y1="172" x2="128" y2="172" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="3"/>
<line x1="50" y1="188" x2="112" y2="188" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="3"/>
<rect x="490" y="148" width="110" height="70" rx="3" fill="#f4f7fa" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="2"/>
<line x1="504" y1="170" x2="582" y2="170" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="3"/>
<line x1="504" y1="186" x2="560" y2="186" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="3"/>
</svg><figcaption>One report stays on the line. The copies do not.</figcaption></figure>
</div></section>
<section class="band"><div class="wrap">
<h2>What the retainer watches</h2>
<div class="cards">
<article class="card"><h3>The definitions</h3><p>The numbers the reports use, and how the tables connect.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Who may change a number</h3><p>And how that change is reviewed before the meeting.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Who can see which rows</h3><p>Updated when people change roles.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Refresh</h3><p>Timed to the close and the operating meeting.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>The list of reports</h3><p>Which one is next, which one should be retired, and whether people still open what you paid for.</p></article>
</div>
</div></section>
<section class="band band-alt"><div class="wrap">
<h2>Who it is for</h2>
<p>A mid-sized company that already has Power BI and wants the reports kept current after the project team leaves.</p>
<p>You still need someone inside the company who can approve a definition. The retainer keeps that definition from quietly changing once the build is over.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="band related-links" aria-labelledby="related-services">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="related-services">Related Power BI Services</h2>
    <ul><li><a href="/power-bi-dashboard-optimization-ai-insights">Dashboard Optimization</a></li>
<li><a href="/data-project-management-change-leadership">Data Project Management</a></li>
<li><a href="/power-bi-training">Power BI Training</a></li></ul>
    <h2>Related Power BI Insights</h2>
    <ul><li><a href="/blog/who-can-change-a-measure">Who can change a measure</a></li>
<li><a href="/blog/row-level-security-who-sees-the-number">Row-level security: who sees the number</a></li>
<li><a href="/blog/gateway-refresh-7am-surprise">Gateway refresh and the 7am surprise</a></li></ul>
  </div>
</section><section class="band band-cta" aria-labelledby="cta-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Next step</p>
    <h2 id="cta-heading">See whether steady care fits.</h2>
    <p class="lede">Book a session. We will look at the report you have now and say whether it needs care or a new build.</p>
    <p class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a Session</a></p>
  </div>
</section></article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
